						"name": "Is there a self-hosted alternative to Google Workspace?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "For the email half, yes — Vectis Mail. It is a self-hosted email server (Postfix, Dovecot, Rspamd) you run on your own VPS, with full IMAP/SMTP mailboxes on your domain, a REST API, inbound webhooks, and DKIM/SPF/DMARC configured by default. Pricing is flat: $0 self-hosted Starter, or $39/month per tenant for Pro, never per user and never per email. The honest caveat: Vectis Mail replaces Gmail and your mail server, not the whole Workspace suite. It does not include Docs, Sheets, Slides, Drive, Meet, or Calendar. If your team lives in those apps, keep them or pair Vectis Mail alongside — Vectis is for organisations that want to own their email and reclaim it from per-seat cloud billing." }
