					},
					{
						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "When does Google Workspace make more sense than self-hosting?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Keep Google Workspace when your team genuinely lives in the suite — real-time Docs/Sheets co-editing and Google Meet are core to how you work — or when you have nobody to run a VPS and 'never think about mail infrastructure' is worth the per-seat premium, or when you are a non-technical organisation that wants one vendor for everything. Self-hosting email means you own deliverability, IP reputation warmup, and uptime. Vectis Mail wins on flat cost, data custody, and zero lock-in; Google Workspace wins on the bundled suite and zero operations. Be honest with yourself about which you actually need." }
